<main class="page">
  <div class="content">
    <a href="/blog" class="back">← Back to Blog</a>
    
    <h1>Pulse v0.11.0: Signal Hydration Fix</h1>
    <span class="date">January 24, 2025</span>
    
    <div class="body">
      <p class="lead">Pulse v0.11.0 is a major release that fixes two critical issues: <strong>signal hydration</strong> for List/Show primitives and <strong>two-way data binding</strong> for form elements. Your forms now work correctly with the createSignal pattern!</p>
      
      <h3>🔧 Problem #1: Content Flash</h3>
      <p>In v0.10.0, pages using List or Show primitives with signal-based state would exhibit a frustrating behavior:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Initial Render:</strong> SSR correctly rendered the content (e.g., list items).</li>
        <li><strong>Hydration:</strong> When JavaScript loaded, the content would briefly flash then disappear!</li>
        <li><strong>Root Cause:</strong> The <code>getProp</code> function evaluated signal expressions and got getter functions instead of actual values.</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h3>📝 Problem #2: Two-Way Binding Broken</h3>
      <p>Form inputs with two-way binding weren't working properly:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Symptom:</strong> Input fields showed literal <code is:raw>{name}</code> instead of actual values.</li>
        <li><strong>Typing:</strong> Changes weren't updating state.</li>
        <li><strong>Setter Functions:</strong> <code>setName</code>, <code>setEmail</code> were not being generated correctly.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>🛠️ Solution: Smart Getter Detection</h3>
      <p>We updated the <code>getProp</code> function to detect signal getter functions and automatically invoke them:</p>
      <pre><code is:raw>// Before (v0.10.0)
let result = eval(expr);
return result; // Returns function, not value!

// After (v0.11.0)
let result = eval(expr);
if (typeof result === 'function' && result.length === 0) {
  result = result(); // Call getter to get value
}
return result;</code></pre>
      
      <h3>✏️ Two-Way Binding Fixes</h3>
      <p>Multiple fixes were applied to make forms work properly:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Property Assignment:</strong> Changed from <code>setAttribute('value', ...)</code> to direct <code>el.value = ...</code> for live DOM updates.</li>
        <li><strong>Setter Extraction:</strong> <code>ScriptParser</code> now extracts both getter AND setter names from <code>createSignal</code> destructuring.</li>
        <li><strong>Event Handling:</strong> Removed automatic <code>e.preventDefault()</code> that was blocking input events.</li>
        <li><strong>Attribute Serialization:</strong> Expression attributes like <code is:raw>value={name}</code> are now correctly passed to the template transformer.</li>
      </ul>
      <pre><code is:raw>// Form Example (Now Works!)
const [name, setName] = createSignal('');
const [email, setEmail] = createSignal('');

// Template
&lt;input value={name} onInput={e => setName(e.target.value)} /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hello, {name}!&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>

      <h3>📐 Template Transformer Fixes</h3>
      <p>The template transformer was also updated to properly wrap primitive attributes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>List each:</strong> Now outputs <code is:raw>each="{items}"</code> instead of <code>each="items"</code></li>
        <li><strong>Show when:</strong> Now outputs <code is:raw>when="{isVisible}"</code> instead of <code>when="isVisible"</code></li>
        <li><strong>SSR Evaluation:</strong> Direct state variable names (not just <code>state.</code> prefix) now work for SSR</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>🚀 createSignal Pattern</h3>
      <p>v0.11.0 fully embraces the <code>createSignal</code> destructuring pattern that's familiar to SolidJS users:</p>
      <pre><code is:raw>// Recommended pattern
const [items, setItems] = createSignal([
  { id: 1, name: 'Apple' },
  { id: 2, name: 'Banana' }
]);

// In template
&lt;List each={items} as="item"&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;{item.name}&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/List&gt;</code></pre>

      <h3>✨ v0.10.0 vs v0.11.0 Comparison</h3>
      <p>A detailed comparison of what changed:</p>
      
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Aspect</th>
              <th>v0.10.0</th>
              <th>v0.11.0</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Signal Hydration</strong></td>
              <td>❌ Broken (returns function)</td>
              <td>✅ Fixed (calls getter)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Two-Way Binding</strong></td>
              <td>❌ Broken (setAttribute)</td>
              <td>✅ Fixed (property assignment)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Form Inputs</strong></td>
              <td>❌ Shows {name} literal</td>
              <td>✅ Shows actual value</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Setter Functions</strong></td>
              <td>❌ Auto-generated incorrectly</td>
              <td>✅ Extracted from destructuring</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>List Primitive</strong></td>
              <td>❌ Flash on load</td>
              <td>✅ Smooth hydration</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Show Primitive</strong></td>
              <td>❌ Flash on load</td>
              <td>✅ Smooth hydration</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>SSR State Names</strong></td>
              <td>Required <code>state.</code> prefix</td>
              <td>Direct names work too</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>📝 Migration Notes</h3>
      <p>To migrate from v0.10.0:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No code changes required:</strong> The fix is entirely in the framework.</li>
        <li><strong>Recommended:</strong> Use <code>createSignal</code> destructuring pattern for all state.</li>
        <li><strong>Forms:</strong> Use <code>onInput</code> for text fields and <code>onChange</code> for select/checkbox.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="alert">
        <strong>⚡ Key Takeaway:</strong> v0.11.0 makes forms and reactive lists work correctly. Two-way binding with createSignal is now fully functional!
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

